  "behavior": [
    "GNU Perl U/L/E modes affect captured backreferences only, persist until switched/end, reset per match and use upstream single-scalar Unicode mappings. Bytes casing is ASCII only. Missing/unset captures are empty; unsupported escapes lose their introducer; dangling escapes are discarded in Perl and ERE. Fixed replacement remains literal.",
    "ASCII word-boundary replacement retains original byte offsets without Vec<char>; actual backspace is a literal regex character. Byte-literal frontend renders escapes with counted admitted opaque-byte storage, preserves invalid bytes, and uses ASCII ignore.case for nonfixed matching.",
    "Readonly WorkspaceText retains actual String capacity and original workspace ticket through consumer lifetime, final publication and runtime teardown. Checked zero-copy UTF8 finish cannot detach the ticket. Buffer growth admits old plus full replacement capacity, reconciles actual allocation, and rolls back or uses exact fallback on preferred growth denial.",
    "Original heap ledger uses the immutable sibling capability without a nested arena lend. Registered mutable-lend regression verifies current-limit denial and same-limit recovery."
